      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "reorder_layers",
  },
  {
    "description": "Start a run that proposes where the text of one variant of an open project goes. The variant needs a visible text layer with text. When the run has succeeded, get_job gives layout.boxes: for each text layer, by its key in slot, x, y, width, height, fontSize, align and color. Nothing is changed by the run; apply the boxes with update_layers. provider is "gemini" (Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, model ID "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"; paid, charged to the user's Google account with no click). Runs are refused unless the user allowed agents for that provider in Adman's Settings. Gives the job ID at once; follow the run with get_job. A run you start makes options for the user to choose from. Leave the choice to the user unless they asked you to choose.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "project_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "provider": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "variant_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "project_id",
        "variant_id",
        "provider",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "propose_layout",
  },
  {
    "description": "Start a run that writes count other texts for one text layer of a variant of an open project (not the headline, which is the campaign message). When the run has succeeded, get_job gives copyOptions, a list of texts. Nothing is changed by the run; put a text on the layer with update_layer. provider is "gemini" (Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, model ID "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"; paid, charged to the user's Google account with no click). Runs are refused unless the user allowed agents for that provider in Adman's Settings. Gives the job ID at once; follow the run with get_job. A run you start makes options for the user to choose from. Leave the choice to the user unless they asked you to choose.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "count": {
          "maximum": 8,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "layer_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "project_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "provider": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "variant_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "project_id",
        "variant_id",
        "layer_id",
        "count",
        "provider",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "copy_options",
  },
  {
    "description": "Start a run that cuts the picture of one picture layer of a variant of an open project out from its background. When the run has succeeded, get_job gives the new picture's asset ID in assetIds. provider is "comfyui" (the user's own ComfyUI server, no charge; the model is BiRefNet). Runs are refused unless the user allowed agents for that provider in Adman's Settings. Gives the job ID at once; follow the run with get_job. A run you start makes options for the user to choose from. Leave the choice to the user unless they asked you to choose.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "layer_id": {
          "minLength": 1,
