        "paths",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "import_assets",
  },
  {
    "description": "Create a campaign in an open project from brief text in JSON, YAML or Markdown, with the same fields as create_campaign’s brief. In Markdown, the first "# " heading is the campaign name, and "Label: value" lines or "## Label" sections give the rest: Region, Audience, Message, Offer, Call to action, Tone, Languages, Sizes, Required words, Prohibited words, Subjects (one "### Name" per subject, with ID, Description and Pictures), and "Copy (fr)", one per language, with Headline and Call to action. For example:
# Spring launch
Region: Canada
Audience: Adults who buy tea online
Message: Warm up slowly
## Subjects
### Tea tin
A subject's pictures are asset IDs from list_assets or full file paths. If any full path is given, the user is asked first and sees each path; you wait up to two minutes, and a refusal is final. Sizes and languages left out are filled as for create_campaign. Gives the campaign ID, its first direction ID, its master variant ID and the subject IDs, and the asset IDs of imported files. A run you start makes options for the user to choose from. Leave the choice to the user unless they asked you to choose.",
    "inputSchema": {
